    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-804c-a738-e5aac950ffc1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "1. Core Concept"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8054-9a41-ceaf505ac1db",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "HTTP methods define the type of action a client wants to perform on a server resource, such as fetching, creating, updating, or deleting data. In Spring Boot, the annotations "
        ],
        [
          "@GetMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@PostMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@PutMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", and "
        ],
        [
          "@DeleteMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " map these HTTP methods to Java methods, making it easy to handle web requests and build RESTful APIs."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8080-8649-c93cfa501022",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-801f-b25e-dfc324609092",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "2. Key Interview Points"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8071-b689-ea4716a6459c",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Purpose of HTTP Methods:",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " Understand what each HTTP method is used for — GET (read), POST (create), PUT (update/replace), DELETE (remove)."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80ff-b6cd-ec25cc3de2c0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot Mapping Annotations:",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " Know how "
        ],
        [
          "@GetMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@PostMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", etc., are shorthand for "
        ],
        [
          "@RequestMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " with specific HTTP methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-803d-8d1b-c0063beee9b6",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Idempotency:",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " GET, PUT, and DELETE are idempotent (calling them multiple times has the same effect as once), but POST is not."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8003-91cc-fdef0466eb7e",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Handling Request and Response:",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " How data is passed (query params, request body) and how responses are returned (JSON, status codes)."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-809b-8218-f764e5e87af6",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-80be-9863-db45269d1963",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "3. Code Example"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8097-93ac-cb9c1546e977",
      "type": "code",
      "richText": [
        [
          "import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;\n\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n@RestController\n@RequestMapping(\"/api/users\")\npublic class UserController {\n\n    private Map<Integer, String> users = new HashMap<>();\n\n    // GET method: Fetch user by id\n    @GetMapping(\"/{id}\")\n    public String getUser(@PathVariable Integer id) {\n        return users.getOrDefault(id, \"User not found\");\n    }\n\n    // POST method: Create a new user\n    @PostMapping(\"/\")\n    public String createUser(@RequestParam Integer id, @RequestParam String name) {\n        users.put(id, name);\n        return \"User created\";\n    }\n\n    // PUT method: Update existing user\n    @PutMapping(\"/{id}\")\n    public String updateUser(@PathVariable Integer id, @RequestParam String name) {\n        if(users.containsKey(id)) {\n            users.put(id, name);\n            return \"User updated\";\n        }\n        return \"User not found\";\n    }\n\n    // DELETE method: Delete user by id\n    @DeleteMapping(\"/{id}\")\n    public String deleteUser(@PathVariable Integer id) {\n        if(users.remove(id) != null) {\n            return \"User deleted\";\n        }\n        return \"User not found\";\n    }\n}\n"
        ]
      ],
      "language": "Java"
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8038-908a-e748e32d590b",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Explanation:",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8038-b6c2-d5e980ba8cc3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " marks the class as a REST API controller, so Spring Boot handles HTTP requests and returns JSON/text responses automatically."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8088-b992-d0d72bfbb59a",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RequestMapping(\"/api/users\")",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " sets the base URL."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-804d-a6df-cbf73ff1599f",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Each mapping annotation corresponds to an HTTP method and maps the URL path to Java methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-803f-873b-d1b7cb762763",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
