    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8005-b7d1-eeec81838823",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A: HTTP methods define the action a client wants to perform on a resource — GET to read, POST to create, PUT to update, and DELETE to remove data. In Spring Boot, the annotations "
        ],
        [
          "@GetMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@PostMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@PutMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", and "
        ],
        [
          "@DeleteMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " map these HTTP requests to Java methods, allowing us to handle these actions easily in REST APIs."
        ]
